# Prism Demonstration Mode — Critical Audit & Enhancement Plan

Kirk, here is the full audit. I've read every line of the demo system. The picture is clear — and your instincts are exactly right.

---

## Executive Summary

The Prism Demonstration Mode has **solid architectural bones** (types, WebSocket plumbing, pause/resume/abort, prompt UI, progress tracking) but suffers from **three systemic failures** that make it appear as a non-functional tab-switcher to the operator:

| Problem | Severity | Root Cause |
|---------|----------|------------|
| **Speed: Too fast for humans** | 🔴 Critical | Default `speedMs = 3000` but tab tour uses `speedMs` directly (~3s per tab); browser demos run even faster because they don't wait for real tool results to render |
| **No visible output** | 🔴 Critical | Demo actions either emit simulated ActivityBus events or call tools whose output is never surfaced to the operator; screenshots are captured but never shown in the overlay |
| **No final report** | 🟡 Major | Demo completes with a generic "Demonstration Complete!" toast — no MD/HTML report, no workspace artifacts, no clickable links, no proof of work |

Additionally, the `demo-scenario-runner.ts` (43 scenarios) is a **separate CLI benchmark** — it doesn't integrate with the interactive dashboard Demo Mode at all, so its thorough scenarios never run in the UI.

